{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"agent_message","text":"R6-F24 appears fixed: unsupported filter versions now produce a warning naming the setting, with no rewrite offered, and a regression test checks that behavior. I’m checking the remaining edge cases, CI wiring, and validation-matrix changes before deciding."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '35,48p' .pose/specs/2026-11-16-pose-doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph.md; sed -n '370,450p' pose-mcp/internal/cli/doctor_commit_graph_test.go; cat .pose/rules/backend-go.md; rg -n 'func RawHistoryGit|SD-28db7861|SD-9fc0fe4e|SD-d29398e6' pose-mcp/internal/pose .pose/review-bundles/rvb-a45e4af11868077d.json; rg -n 'commit.graph|commit-graph' .pose/knowledge\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '35,48p' .pose/specs/2026-11-16-pose-doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph.md; sed -n '370,450p' pose-mcp/internal/cli/doctor_commit_graph_test.go; cat .pose/rules/backend-go.md; rg -n 'func RawHistoryGit|SD-28db7861|SD-9fc0fe4e|SD-d29398e6' pose-mcp/internal/pose .pose/review-bundles/rvb-a45e4af11868077d.json; rg -n 'commit.graph|commit-graph' .pose/knowledge\"","aggregated_output":"---\n\n## 2. Requirements\n\n### Functional\n- R1: When the project root is a Git repository whose HEAD has at least 500 commits, and Git's own trace of a last-commit lookup by path shows no changed-path Bloom filter consulted, `pose doctor` shall report the check `git.commit-graph` at level `next`, with the command that writes it, the same command the fix runs; the judgement follows whichever commit-graph Git loads (its own object directory or an alternate, a single file or a chain).\n- R2: `pose doctor --fix --yes` shall remediate `git.commit-graph` by running `git commit-graph write --reachable --changed-paths --max-new-filters=-1` in the project root, so `commitGraph.maxNewFilters` cannot leave commits without filters, after which the check shall report `ok`.\n- R3: A repository with fewer than 500 commits on HEAD, or one whose last-commit lookup Git answers from the filters, shall report `ok`; a project root that is not a Git repository, has no commit on HEAD, has a shallow history or has no file in HEAD's tree shall not report the check; Git warnings printed by a successful lookup, such as an unreadable commit-graph, shall report `warn`; no diagnostic command shall fetch from a remote; any other failure to read the state shall report `warn` with a bounded description of the failure; when Git configuration keeps it from reading commit-graphs or their changed-path filters, `pose doctor` shall report `git.commit-graph-reads` at `warn`, naming the setting, instead of recommending a rewrite.\n- R4: The pose-dist CI jobs that check out the full history shall write the commit-graph with changed paths before their gates.\n\n### Non-functional\n- A verificação roda três comandos Git de leitura e uma busca do último commit de um arquivo com o trace2 ligado.\n\n### Security\n\tif f := doctorCommitGraphFinding(t, repo); f.Level != \"warn\" {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"an unreadable commit-graph under a short history: %+v\", f)\n\t}\n}\n\n// Review F22: a HEAD without files is not applicable under a short history\n// too.\nfunc TestDoctorCommitGraphSkipsAShortEmptyTree(t *testing.T) {\n\trepo := shortHistoryRepo(t)\n\tgitInRepo(t, repo, \"rm\", \"-q\", \"-r\", \"--\", \".\")\n\tgitInRepo(t, repo, \"-c\", \"user.name=fixture\", \"-c\", \"user.email=fixture@example.invalid\", \"-c\", \"commit.gpgsign=false\", \"commit\", \"-q\", \"-m\", \"empty\")\n\tif _, err := readCommitGraphState(repo); !errors.Is(err, errCommitGraphNotApplicable) {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a short history with an empty HEAD tree: %v, want not applicable\", err)\n\t}\n}\n\n// Review F23: the command doctor shows is the one its fix runs, and\n// following it by hand writes the filters under commitGraph.maxNewFilters=0.\nfunc TestDoctorCommitGraphShowsTheEffectiveCommand(t *testing.T) {\n\trepo := longHistoryRepo(t, nil)\n\tgitInRepo(t, repo, \"config\", \"commitGraph.maxNewFilters\", \"0\")\n\tremoveCommitGraph(t, repo)\n\tf := doctorCommitGraphFinding(t, repo)\n\tif f.Level != \"next\" || !strings.Contains(f.Hint, \"'\"+commitGraphWriteCommand+\"'\") {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the shown command is not the fix's: %+v\", f)\n\t}\n\targs := strings.Fields(strings.TrimPrefix(commitGraphWriteCommand, \"git \"))\n\tgitInRepo(t, repo, args...)\n\tstate, err := readCommitGraphState(repo)\n\tif err != nil || !state.filtersUsed {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"following the shown command under maxNewFilters=0: %+v %v\", state, err)\n\t}\n}\n\n// Review F24: an unsupported commitGraph.changedPathsVersion keeps Git from\n// reading the filters; doctor names it instead of recommending a rewrite.\nfunc TestDoctorCommitGraphNamesAnUnsupportedVersion(t *testing.T) {\n\trepo := longHistoryRepo(t, nil)\n\tgitInRepo(t, repo, \"config\", \"commitGraph.changedPathsVersion\", \"3\")\n\tvar reads doctorFinding\n\tinDir(t, repo, func() {\n\t\tvar out, errB bytes.Buffer\n\t\tMain([]string{\"doctor\", \"--json\"}, &out, &errB)\n\t\tvar report doctorJSON\n\t\tif err := json.Unmarshal(out.Bytes(), &report); err != nil {\n\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"invalid JSON: %v\", err)\n\t\t}\n\t\tfor _, f := range report.Findings {\n\t\t\tif f.Check == \"git.commit-graph\" {\n\t\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"a rewrite is recommended under an unsupported version: %+v\", f)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tif f.Check == \"git.commit-graph-reads\" {\n\t\t\t\treads = f\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t})\n\tif reads.Level != \"warn\" || !strings.Contains(reads.Message, \"commitGraph.changedPathsVersion=3\") {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"an unsupported changedPathsVersion: %+v\", reads)\n\t}\n}\n# Rule: Backend Go\n\n## When to consult\n\nConsult this guide for HTTP handlers, domain services, persistence, concurrency, and integrations between Go services.\n\n## Required patterns\n\n- Handle and propagate errors with enough context for diagnosis.\n- Validate handler input and return HTTP status codes consistent with the contract.\n- Keep business rules in service or domain layers, not in transport code.\n- Honor `context.Context` for timeouts and cancellation.\n- Put data access behind clear interfaces that support testing.\n- Use structured logs without exposing sensitive data.\n\n## Blocking anti-patterns\n\n- Ignoring error returns, including `_` for critical errors.\n- Using `panic` in ordinary request flows instead of controlled error handling.\n- Coupling handlers directly to concrete repository implementations without an abstraction.\n- Running unbounded or unpaginated queries in potentially large endpoints.\n- Introducing concurrency without adequate synchronization or race protection.\n\n## Minimum checks\n\n- Run `go test ./...` in the affected scope.\n- Run `go test -race ./...` when concurrency changes.\n- Run `go vet ./...` without blocking findings.\n- Run the applicable Go lint check, such as `golangci-lint`, without critical errors.\n\n## Precedence in multi-domain conflicts\n\n- Apply the most restrictive security, contract, and operational rule when domain rules conflict.\n- Prefer verifiable check evidence and explicit risk mitigation when speed conflicts with control.\n- Record the precedence decision and objective rationale in the review.\n\n## Recurrence traceability\n\n> Also apply: [.pose/rules/_base-recurrence.md](_base-recurrence.md)\nrg: .pose/review-bundles/rvb-a45e4af11868077d.json: No such file or directory (os error 2)\npose-mcp/internal/pose/spec_trailers.go:75:func RawHistoryGit(root string, args ...string) *exec.Cmd {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/spec_trailers.go:80:func RawHistoryGitContext(ctx context.Context, root string, args ...string) *exec.Cmd {\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
