{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"git show 5c1c5658 -- .pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json; git show 2e30bb53 -- .pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json; git show ac7610d7 -- .pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json; sed -n '135,145p' .pose/specs/2026-11-16-pose-doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph.md\"","aggregated_output":"commit 5c1c5658becae1f03fcbfc20fff15af65cfc8879\nAuthor: Oseias Pereira <oseiaspereira88@gmail.com>\nDate:   Mon Nov 16 13:08:37 2026 -0300\n\n    fix(doctor): ask Git whether it uses the changed-path filters\n    \n    Round 1 review findings F2-F4 came from reading commit-graph files by hand:\n    alternates were ignored, a chain was preferred to the single graph Git\n    loads first, and unsupported or truncated files were accepted. Doctor now\n    runs one last-commit lookup with GIT_TRACE2_EVENT and looks for Git's bloom\n    statistics, so the graph Git loads is judged by Git's rules. F5: only a\n    missing repository or an unborn HEAD skips the check; any other failure is a\n    warning with a bounded reason.\n    \n    POSE-Spec: pose-doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph\n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018BdzfqwBXh8UdZwnt129jD\n\ndiff --git a/.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json b/.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\nindex edd39bcb..bb92d120 100644\n--- a/.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\n+++ b/.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\n@@ -2422,7 +2422,7 @@\n         {\n           \"name\": \"doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph-integration\",\n           \"program\": \"go\",\n-          \"args\": [\"test\", \"./internal/cli\", \"-run\", \"TestDoctorRecommendsTheCommitGraph\", \"-count=1\"],\n+          \"args\": [\"test\", \"./internal/cli\", \"-run\", \"TestDoctorRecommendsTheCommitGraph|TestDoctorCommitGraphReportsAnUnreadableHistory\", \"-count=1\"],\n           \"severity\": \"required\",\n           \"evidenceClass\": \"integration\"\n         },\ncommit 2e30bb5396e886c0c91b9b4cff2d70ef89380b87\nAuthor: Oseias Pereira <oseiaspereira88@gmail.com>\nDate:   Mon Nov 16 14:08:57 2026 -0300\n\n    fix(doctor): tell unborn from broken, probe literally, name disabled reads\n    \n    Round 2 review findings. F6: only a non-repository and an unborn HEAD skip\n    the check; a HEAD whose commit cannot be read, or a repository Git cannot\n    open, is a warning. F7: the probe runs with GIT_LITERAL_PATHSPECS=1, so a\n    first file named like pathspec syntax is looked up as itself. F8: when\n    core.commitGraph, commitGraph.readChangedPaths or changedPathsVersion keep\n    Git from reading the filters, doctor names the setting in\n    git.commit-graph-reads instead of recommending a rewrite that cannot help.\n    \n    POSE-Spec: pose-doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph\n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018BdzfqwBXh8UdZwnt129jD\n\ndiff --git a/.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json b/.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\nindex bfcc28e6..3d3fa181 100644\n--- a/.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\n+++ b/.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\n@@ -2422,7 +2422,7 @@\n         {\n           \"name\": \"doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph-integration\",\n           \"program\": \"go\",\n-          \"args\": [\"test\", \"./internal/cli\", \"-run\", \"TestDoctorRecommendsTheCommitGraph|TestDoctorCommitGraphReportsAnUnreadableHistory\", \"-count=1\"],\n+          \"args\": [\"test\", \"./internal/cli\", \"-run\", \"TestDoctorRecommendsTheCommitGraph|TestDoctorCommitGraphReportsAnUnreadableHistory|TestDoctorCommitGraphTellsUnbornFromBroken|TestDoctorCommitGraphProbesALiteralPath|TestDoctorCommitGraphNamesDisabledReads\", \"-count=1\"],\n           \"severity\": \"required\",\n           \"evidenceClass\": \"integration\"\n         },\ncommit ac7610d7a9792ef12a072c0021fec8d038de63ba\nAuthor: Oseias Pereira <oseiaspereira88@gmail.com>\nDate:   Mon Nov 16 17:54:02 2026 -0300\n\n    fix(doctor): skip shallow and empty trees, never fetch, surface Git warnings\n    \n    Round 5 review findings F15-F20. A shallow history and a HEAD without files\n    are not applicable. The fix writes filters for every commit\n    (--max-new-filters=-1). commitGraph.changedPathsVersion is read before the\n    deprecated readChangedPaths, as Git does. Diagnostics run with\n    GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1, so a partial clone reports missing objects instead of\n    fetching. A warning Git prints while a lookup succeeds, such as an\n    unreadable commit-graph, is a doctor warning.\n    \n    POSE-Spec: pose-doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph\n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018BdzfqwBXh8UdZwnt129jD\n\ndiff --git a/.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json b/.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\nindex 9d463bb3..5910b464 100644\n--- a/.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\n+++ b/.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\n@@ -2429,7 +2429,7 @@\n         {\n           \"name\": \"doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph-integration\",\n           \"program\": \"go\",\n-          \"args\": [\"test\", \"./internal/cli\", \"-run\", \"TestDoctorRecommendsTheCommitGraph|TestDoctorCommitGraphReportsAnUnreadableHistory|TestDoctorCommitGraphTellsUnbornFromBroken|TestDoctorCommitGraphProbesALiteralPath|TestDoctorCommitGraphNamesDisabledReads\", \"-count=1\"],\n+          \"args\": [\"test\", \"./internal/cli\", \"-run\", \"TestDoctorRecommendsTheCommitGraph|TestDoctorCommitGraph\", \"-count=1\"],\n           \"severity\": \"required\",\n           \"evidenceClass\": \"integration\"\n         },\n- R2 [satisfied] test:TestDoctorRecommendsTheCommitGraph test:TestDoctorCommitGraphFixIgnoresMaxNewFilters test:TestDoctorCommitGraphShowsTheEffectiveCommand\n- R3 [satisfied] test:TestDoctorRecommendsTheCommitGraph test:TestDoctorCommitGraphReportsAnUnreadableHistory test:TestDoctorCommitGraphTellsUnbornFromBroken test:TestDoctorCommitGraphNamesDisabledReads test:TestDoctorCommitGraphSkipsAShallowClone test:TestDoctorCommitGraphSkipsAnEmptyTree test:TestDoctorCommitGraphFollowsConfigurationPrecedence test:TestDoctorCommitGraphNeverFetches test:TestDoctorCommitGraphReportsAnUnreadableGraph test:TestDoctorCommitGraphWarnsBelowTheThreshold test:TestDoctorCommitGraphSkipsAShortEmptyTree test:TestDoctorCommitGraphNamesAnUnsupportedVersion\n- R4 [satisfied] O passo `Write the Git commit-graph with changed-path filters` nos dois jobs de `.github/workflows/ci.yml` que fazem checkout do histórico inteiro.\n\n### Known gaps\n- Nenhuma.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Final Report\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport subprocess,json\nfor version in ['-1','0','1','2','3']:\n p=subprocess.run(['git','--no-replace-objects','-c','commitGraph.changedPathsVersion='+version,'log','-1','--format=%H','--','AGENTS.md'],env={'PATH':'/usr/bin:/bin','GIT_TRACE2_EVENT':'1','GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH':'1','GIT_GRAFT_FILE':'/dev/null'},text=True,capture_output=True)\n events=[]\n for s in p.stderr.splitlines():\n  try:\n   e=json.loads(s)\n   if e.get('category')=='bloom':events.append(e.get('value'))\n  except ValueError: pass\n print(version,p.returncode,events)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
